  "query_preview": "..Partly to mostly cloudy conditions prevailed early\nthis morning with a few storms occurring west of Picacho Peak. \nThis weekend will see isolated to scattered thunderstorms with \nthe usual threats, gusty outflow winds and brief heavy rain. \n\nMonday, at this time, looks to be a bit more active possibly\nassociated with a weak disturbance moving north across the area.\nQPF is trending up with WPC placing portions of the forecast\narea under slight risk for excessive rainfall with the potential\nfor stronger storms producing rainfall rates of 1-2\"/hr leading\nto the increased risk of localized flash flooding. Time will\ntell as its difficult to time disturbances this far out.\n\nWill keep daily threat of afternoon/evening storms Tuesday\nthru Friday with day-to-day changes in areal coverage.\n\nHigh temperatures will mostly be around normal for the next 7\ndays.",
